-- Q14250: Financial Valuation Methods [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 805-20-30-1, WARA should approximate WACC when the PPA is internally consistent. When WARA (excluding goodwill) falls below WACC, goodwill — as the residual asset carrying the highest implied return — bridges the gap, which is the expected and normal outcome in a properly performed PPA.
Wrong (A): A lower WARA does not indicate overstated asset values; tangible and intangible assets inherently carry lower risk than the overall enterprise.
Wrong (B): This describes the normal relationship correctly but is not what the WARA-below-WACC gap indicates — it is the expected outcome, not a separate finding.
Wrong (C): A lower WARA means individual asset discount rates are appropriate; if they were too high, WARA would exceed WACC rather than fall below it.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14250;

