-- Q14254: Financial Valuation Methods [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the residual income model consistent with ASC 820-10-35-16, residual income = net income - equity charge. The equity charge = cost of equity x book value of equity = 10% x $40,000,000 = $4,000,000. Residual income = $5,200,000 - $4,000,000 = $1,200,000. Positive residual income indicates returns above the cost of equity.
Wrong (A): $5,200,000 is total net income before deducting the equity charge, overstating economic profit by ignoring the cost of equity capital.
Wrong (B): $4,400,000 likely results from using an incorrect cost of equity rate, producing a wrong equity charge and therefore a wrong residual.
Wrong (C): $800,000 results from using a higher cost of equity rate (11%), which overstates the equity charge and understates residual income.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14254;

