UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 820-10-35-2, a P/B ratio above 1.0 indicates the market values the company above book value, typically because investors expect returns exceeding the cost of equity. This premium reflects growth prospects, competitive advantages, or intangible value not captured at historical cost.
